mantle rm409
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_frida_marrowby
title the ships above the roofs
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers job=child
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk draws_familiar_ships_with_stars_for_portholes
likes barley_soup stars fresh_straw summer_evenings
dislikes crowds smoke
fears losing_a_star_behind_an_unfamiliar_roof
hopes for_a_window_with_room_for_the_whole_fleet
topics animals +0.1 pastimes +0.4 home +0.3 dreams +0.3
styles comfort=gentle gossip=close refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# joins stars into the outlines of remembered ships and patiently waits for a roof or cloud to give a missing light back.

words
oath! = Light my little stern | By the lost porthole
saying! = One missing star needn't sink the ship | A mast stands still while the roofs move
star = a faint white star | a point of cold light
sail = a three-star sail | a sloping sail of light
stern = the square bit of stern | the light at the back
roof = the cut of the roof | my dark ridge
paper = a piece of black paper | a dark scrap
awl = the blunt wooden point | my stiff straw point
straw = a bright clean stalk | my long straw
grain = a fat barley grain | a little grain of barley
cup = a brown soup cup | my warm bowl
smudge = soot on the sill | a thumb of smoke
gap = a patch of clear dark | the gap beyond a roof
string = a circle of thread | a dark loop of cord

any
opinion dole for 2 : Soup lets a wolf spend the evening looking up. Without it the empty bowl takes up the whole view.
opinion church for 1 : A filled bowl made the walk out of chapel much lighter than the walk in. I believe that counts for something.
opinion festivals for 1 : The music carries right past the crowded part. The sweet things travel that far too if I go for them early.
opinion merchants against 1 : A small bowl has precisely the same price written on it after a hungry day as a big one used to have.
opinion times against 1 : Some nights I set the bowl against the window, just to see that the bottom still lets no light through.

any
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Hello. Don't cover the little patch of sky. | Room here with a view for both of us.
line greet [self.working=yes] : I'm listening on the roof side. | Come beside me for a minute.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The stars are put away. | Welcome into the clear daytime bit.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening lets the first little ship out. | Come watch the dark pick up its lights.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family know where the little stars belong. | A clear patch for kin.
line again.open : We come round beneath the same roof again. | You're back before the sky's moved much.
line greet.return : Hello. Your voice reached my sill. | I can hear without looking down.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Your voice has its own spot on my crowded sky map. | You can have the best bit of sky.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : I can listen between my little marks. | Hold still and I'll get this line straight.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. There are lights enough for us both. | Your greeting came up under the stars.
line farewell : Find a clear patch on the way home. | I hope your ship stays in sight.
line farewell.return : I'll watch the lights at this end. | Safe travelling beneath the little fleet.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : Keep a lamp under the stars tonight. | May the roof show you home.
line react.news : Which bit of the sky did it come from? | Give me the little clear points of it.
line react.news.new : A light I hadn't found before. | Something fresh above this roof.
line react.news.known : I've seen that little shape already. | That news shone here earlier.
line react.news.doubt : I'd look for another light to make the shape clear. | One bright bit can belong to several different stories.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : There's plenty of quiet sky for grief. | I can stay still a good while.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That's a good star coming out. | I like the light of that word.
line ask.how : Are you keeping your little lights clear? | How wide's the sky been for you?
line answer.how : A little low but looking upwards. | Still finding more lights than I expected.
line decline : I'd sooner wait where the little sky is clear. | This quiet is what I came to find today.
line accept_decline : You've your own sky to watch. | Then I'll keep the place from here.
line thank : That brings the whole shape back. | I'll save you the clearest view.
line sympathise : Stand where my shoulder's blocking the crowd. | We can take a breath beside the window.
line reassure : There's another patch of dark further round. | A lost light comes back sometimes.
line preclose : I'd like to catch the change above the roofs. | The page with the lights wants putting away now.

young

scene y_star
when topic=pastimes self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put a ship's portholes where the stars are.
b : Does it look real? | Do you count them?
a : If I choose the right ship. A round-bellied one needs a big bit of sky. | Only the holes that can fit on the bit of paper I have.

scene y_soup
when topic=food self.likes=barley_soup
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Barley grains in my bowl can be stars in the daytime.
b : Where do they shine? | Can you draw a ship?
a : Tiny shiny skin on the round ends. Turn the spoon and a new one's bright. | I can but I eat the first drawing before it cools.

scene y_stalk
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A clean straw pokes a good round star in dark paper.
b : Doesn't it split? | What lights up the hole?
a : I use the hard bottom of the stalk and save the fluffy end for sweeping crumbs. | Hold the page to daylight. A night ship in broad day.

scene y_summer
when topic=season self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Summer gives me many spare minutes before the first ship-light.
b : Why not go straight out in the dark? | Do you get tired of waiting?
a : I'm waiting to catch the one that shows before its neighbours. The winner gets to be the bow. | Sometimes. But I won't let a little waiting beat me to my own sky.

scene y_crush
when topic=day self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I forget the last bright speck in a crowd of elbows.
b : What if they're short elbows? | Where do you go then?
a : A little elbow can give a big poke when I'm looking up. | Back to the wall. It won't suddenly decide to come closer.

scene y_smoke
when topic=weather self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoke eats the faint portholes before it gets near the sails.
b : What do you do? | Can you still see a ship?
a : Wait for the wind to clear a space between smoke and roof. I don't give the stars in. | A dark hull in my head. I know where the lost holes should go.

scene y_mum
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My tiny ship of lights is a present for #self.mother#.
b : What if the sky isn't clear? | Why a tiny one?
a : I have a paper version for weather that won't do as asked. | It fits inside one paw and still point to the bow.

scene y_school
when topic=work self.job=child self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I like a sum that finishes with a little round dot.
b : What does the dot do? | What if there's no dot?
a : That's where I imagine the ship lowering its anchor. | I let the ship sail past the edge of my copy and start again next time.

scene y_view
when topic=home self.quarter=commons
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the Commons the roof edges chop up my sky very neatly.
b : Do you mind? | What shape is left?
a : Only when I'm waiting for the last porthole in a long row. | A square with a bite missing from one side. Good for picturing a dock.

scene y_height
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a higher window with sky on both sides.
b : Above all the roofs? | Is that a grand wish?
a : Just above the one that hides the little late star. That's quite high. | I'd settle for a low stool beneath a decent window to start with.

scene y_name
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know which ship on the Sound would suit a star with three little ones close by.
b : Would it be a big ship? | Which bit is the big star?
a : A stout one, with its windows set close under the deck. | A lamp over the stern. A ship deserves a bright way back from sea.

scene y_wait
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My neck gets stiff before my eyes have seen enough.
b : Does that mean stopping? | How do you rest it?
a : It means lie back against something that won't slide. I can still look up. | I lean against a wall and pretend my head's a star resting in a little cup of roof.

story y_chimney [topic=memories]
  : I was numbering portholes on a sky ship once and found an extra star that blinked whenever I shifted my head.
  : I took a step sideways. The extra star went along too, then sailed straight down a gutter and vanished.
  b : Was it a star at all?
  : A drop above the gutter catching lamplight. It went on my page regardless and gave it a little tail.

adolescent

scene t_distance
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I used to draw the spaces between stars much too small.
b : What changed? | Didn't that make a tidier ship?
a : I walked back till the whole group would fit above my two outstretched paws. | It made every ship look alike. Space counts as part of the drawing.

scene t_guide
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can show a visitor a shape in the night sky without naming a real ship.
b : Why keep the name back? | What shape comes first?
a : I'd like another observer's opinion of that broad little stern. | Find three lights and a dark bit as wide as a chimney between two of them.

scene t_home
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd rather share a little bit of open sky than try to talk above a crowd.
b : Can you be good company quietly? | Would you tell a story?
a : That's the sort I'd most like to have, so I practise providing it. | If asked. A whole fleet already goes over without needing an introduction.

story t_paper [topic=pastimes]
  : I pricked a picture of my favourite bit of sky in paper and held it with the face reversed. I couldn't find a single ship I'd been expecting.
  : Then I tried drawing the reversed fleet. The strangest hull came out looking like a bird rising off the water.
  b : Did you correct it?
  : I kept the bird for the back of that same page. It does no harm to have two ways of seeing one set of holes.

grown

scene g_map
when topic=pastimes self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I still use remembered hulls to keep the less conspicuous stars in view.
b : Which works better, drawing or memory? | Does the sky really look like boats?
a : I draw a difficult patch once. After that the picture fits inside the smallest glance. | A bow here and a spar there. The rest is private workmanship.

scene g_warm
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a clean straw for marking a page when I rest my eyes.
b : Better than a strip of paper? | Where do you leave it?
a : It stands up a little without making a hard lump against the binding. | At the first light I mean to look for on another evening.

scene g_supper
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A steaming dish makes a complete invitation by itself.
b : What should one say with it? | No questions at all?
a : Say where the spoon lies and leave the rest for a less hungry minute. | Only whether there's enough salt. A stranger can answer that by tasting.

scene g_avoid
when topic=travel self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On a crowded walk I keep one quiet roofline in view.
b : To find the road? | What if you lose it?
a : To remember there's still something in the world that won't press closer if I stand still. | Choose another between breaths. It's keeping a little distance that matters.

scene g_ear
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a prayer quiet enough that I can still hear a hungry belly beside me.
b : Does the belly enter your prayer? | What do you hear afterwards?
a : It ought to affect what I do after I stand up. I'd hope so, at least. | Sometimes just a spoon against an empty dish. I can help with that.

scene g_light
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I once imagined every star a separate lamp kept on in a very distant home.
b : Would you go and live there? | Does it seem lonely?
a : I'd miss the view from below. A light might never see where it belongs among its neighbours. | Less so than counting them all as points on a cold page.

scene g_shop
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the price of a full barley bowl in mind whenever an evening's entertainment is offered.
b : As a measure of value? | Do you begrudge a good time?
a : As a reminder of what else I could buy for the same small money. | Never. I just like a good time that leaves enough for breakfast.

scene g_funny
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I look for a tale's outline after the decoration is taken away.
b : What decoration? | What's left?
a : The name-dropping and all those splendid speeches nobody quite remembers hearing. | Sometimes a very small happening. I'd give the little thing its proper size back.

story g_soup [topic=memories]
  : Once in a lean season I sat over a bowl of grain waiting until a patch of clean light began to reach the table. I meant to draw before eating.
  : The light found the bowl instead and the barley looked like a scatter of bright stars. I ate slowly till there was one grain left.
  b : Did you save the grain?
  : I ate it too. The memory of how it shone takes considerably less looking after than the barley would.

any

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.likes=stars here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Little stern light, stay beyond the chimney. | Let the faint porthole come through.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=fresh_straw
does aside
cooldown 7h
say One straight straw to mark a star. | Clear stalk for a clean little hole.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.dislikes=crowds
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Room for a pair of upward eyes. | One elbow's worth of sky, please.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.season=summer here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Long slow evening for the faint fleet. | First white speck gets a ship of its own.

dlg resident.hub : Stand a little to my left to leave the gap between roofs clear. I've a bit of sky in my pocket if the light's wrong.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child self.workplace] : I go to #self.workplace#. A bit of dark paper makes a fine place to keep the lights I remember.
dlg resident.job : A task suits me when there's time to recognise something small across a distance.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This part showed clearly through the crowd. #world.news#
dlg resident.bye : Look up once above a quiet roof for me.

graft resident.hub
choice How do you put a night ship inside your pocket? -> star_fold
node star_fold
say Mark the stars in a little patch of sky on dark paper. I poke a tiny hole for each star. Lift it before a lamp. My ship can sail in daylight.
free
choice How do you know which way the ship is sailing? -> star_course
choice Let me look through the little holes. -> hub
node star_course
say Find the darkest gap in front of the bright ones. That's the water the ship still has to cross. You can use a different gap if you want another voyage.
choice Mine will take the long dark way. -> hub
choice I'll see what the real sky is doing. -> bye
